    "check": "every name and figure read from the page image"
  },
  "note": "Election of the whole council of nine on Wednesday 15 January 1908: fifteen candidates (eighteen had been nominated, Northern Whig weekly, 11 January 1908). \"The Unionists gained a sweeping victory in this town, for of the nine seats vacant eight were won by members of that party.\" Only the elected are given with votes. The Irish News names the two defeated Nationalists, Michael M'Crudden and Patrick Burns (no figures); the other four defeated candidates are not named. The Northern Whig prints \"J. Searon\" (the Irish News has J. Feron, the nominations John Fearon); the Irish News gives Neill as J. Neill and Jackson as T. Jackson (nominated as F. S. Jackson). The Irish News says the poll turned on the Mourne water scheme: Coburn, Meredith, Fearon, Boyle, Jackson and Neill supported it, Gamble, Crothers and Dickson opposed it. Returning officer F. Sterling; legal assessor W. H. Atkinson."
}
